{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-04-Jul-2024-Shift4.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "22%", "added": false}, {"text": "27%", "added": false}, {"text": "30%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "The ratio of the lateral surface area to the total surface area of a cylinder with base diameter 60cm and height 10 cm is:", "options": [{"text": "1:9", "added": false}, {"text": "1:7", "added": false}, {"text": "1:4", "added": false}, {"text": "1:3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "9.6 hrs and 84 marks", "added": false}, {"text": "6.4 hrs and 84 marks", "added": false}, {"text": "40 hrs and 21 marks", "added": false}, {"text": "6.4 hrs and 90 marks", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "From a circle, a sector with a central angle of 30° is cut off. If the length of the arc of this sector is 5.5 cm, then find the radius (in cm) of the circle.", "options": [{"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "10.5", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "140", "added": false}, {"text": "310", "added": false}, {"text": "450", "added": false}, {"text": "224", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "For what positive values of k do the following pair of linear equations have infinitely many solutions? kx + 3y – ( k – 3 ) = 0 12x + ky – k = 0", "options": [{"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "The following bar graph represents the production of three types of buses by a company over the years (in thousands). In which of the following years was the percentage production of B type buses to C type buses, the maximum?", "options": [{"text": "2015", "added": false}, {"text": "2013", "added": false}, {"text": "2016", "added": false}, {"text": "2014", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "If the price of tea is increased by 40%, by how what percentage must the consumption of tea be decreased so as not to increase the expenditure?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "An amount of ₹8,000 was invested for 2 years, partly in scheme 1 at the rate of 5% simple interest per annum and the rest in scheme 2 at the rate of 4% simple interest per annum. The total interest received at the end was ₹720. The amount of money invested in scheme 1 is:", "options": [{"text": "₹3,640", "added": false}, {"text": "₹7,200", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4,400", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "In a circle, O is the centre and AOB is the diameter. AT is a tangent to the circle. Line TB intersects the circle at Q. Given that ∠ AOQ = 94°, find ∠ ATQ.", "options": [{"text": "86°", "added": false}, {"text": "43°", "added": false}, {"text": "47°", "added": false}, {"text": "133°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "A shopkeeper buys 1800 kg wheat for ₹32,400. If 20% of this wheat is spoiled due to rain, at what rate (₹/kg) should he sell the rest to earn 20%?", "options": [{"text": "29", "added": false}, {"text": "26", "added": false}, {"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "Two parallel chords of length 5 units and 8 units are on opposite sides of the center of a circle of radius 7 units. What is the distance between the chords? (round your answer to two decimal places)", "options": [{"text": "11.82 units", "added": false}, {"text": "12.28 units", "added": false}, {"text": "11.28 units", "added": false}, {"text": "12.82 units", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "In a triangle ABC, AB = AC. BC is extended to D such that CD = AB and the angle ADC is 30°. What are the angles of triangle ABC?", "options": [{"text": "30°, 60°, 90°", "added": false}, {"text": "50°, 60°, 70°", "added": false}, {"text": "60°, 60°, 60°", "added": false}, {"text": "45°, 60°, 75°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "If the income of Neha is 5% more than that of Monica, then the income of Monica is what percentage less than that of Neha?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "What is the smallest number that must be added to 19487161 so that it is divisible by 11?", "options": [{"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "3 solid spheres of diameters 6 cm, 8 cm and 10 cm are melted together to form a single solid sphere. Find its radius.", "options": [{"text": "12 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "9 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "3 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "6 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "conversion-and-melting", "key_answer": null}]}